\title{data.table.ext: Enhanced Display, Sampling, and 'DuckDB' Querying for 'data.table'}
\description{
Adds opt-in data.table output enhancements for printing, grouped sampling, and data.table-focused str() and dput() behavior, including helpers for grouped value highlighting and readability improvements. Also provides a data.table-style '[i, j, by]' interface backed by 'DuckDB', translating expressions to SQL and executing them inside 'DuckDB' so data never needs to be pulled into R until the result is materialized as a data.table. Also reverse-engineers a database into a data model -- tables, columns, keys and references -- and draws it as an interactive entity-relationship diagram that builds the query for the tables and columns you pick.
